cruise.desc.body_light=Light body for short and medium game distances.
cruise.detail.body_light=220 mass limit. No high-output engine, extended tank or penetrator.
cruise.desc.body_classic=Versatile body for different warheads and ground/air launch.
cruise.detail.body_classic=Maximum mass: 520 game units.
cruise.desc.body_heavy=Large body for heavier payloads and extra fuel.
cruise.detail.body_heavy=Maximum mass: 900 game units.
cruise.desc.engine_economy=Low fuel consumption, limited thrust and speed.
cruise.detail.engine_economy=Best for a light build; extra mass reduces acceleration.
cruise.desc.engine_standard=Balanced thrust, speed and fuel consumption.
cruise.detail.engine_standard=Speed and acceleration depend on the complete missile mass.
cruise.desc.engine_fast=More thrust and speed, but heavier and fuel-hungry.
cruise.detail.engine_fast=Not compatible with the light body.
cruise.desc.fuel_short=Small fuel reserve with minimum added mass.
cruise.detail.fuel_short=For short missions and lightweight builds.
cruise.desc.fuel_standard=Balanced fuel reserve and mass.
cruise.detail.fuel_standard=Range also depends on engine, wings and total mass.
cruise.desc.fuel_extended=Extra range, lower speed due to additional mass.
cruise.detail.fuel_extended=Not compatible with the light body.
cruise.desc.wings_compact=Compact span and low mass.
cruise.detail.wings_compact=Reduced range; air or rail launch.
cruise.desc.wings_range=Extended span increases flight range.
cruise.detail.wings_range=Extra mass and reduced turning rate.
cruise.desc.wings_folding=Compact before launch, deploy in flight.
cruise.detail.wings_folding=Required for a ground booster.
cruise.desc.nav_coordinate=Fly almost straight toward the goal, no obstacle planning.
cruise.detail.nav_coordinate=Obstacles can cause an impact.
cruise.desc.nav_route=Choose altitude and local bypasses, check the next leg and remember the avoidance side.
cruise.detail.nav_route=Individual smooth route when fuel permits; route variation ends before the strike.
cruise.desc.nav_terrain=Terrain probes, more avoidance directions and manoeuvre memory; stronger target tracking.
cruise.detail.nav_terrain=Separated friendly salvo corridors toward nearby targets; known-terrain bypasses. Respects fuel reserve.
cruise.desc.seeker_none=Attack one programmed coordinate.
cruise.detail.seeker_none=Entity search and multiple search areas are unavailable.
cruise.desc.seeker_optical=Visible targets of the chosen category; line of sight required. Night and rain reduce range.
cruise.detail.seeker_optical=Requires line of sight; enables search-area mode.
cruise.desc.seeker_thermal=Wider thermal search for living targets and vehicles; works at night but flares can distract it.
cruise.detail.seeker_thermal=Requires line of sight; flares can break target lock.
cruise.desc.seeker_radar=Wide-sector WarTech ground/air vehicle search; blocked by solid terrain and affected by jamming.
cruise.detail.seeker_radar=Strong electronic jamming suppresses acquisition.
cruise.desc.warhead_he=General-purpose explosion on fuse activation.
cruise.detail.warhead_he=Contact, delayed and airburst fuses.
cruise.desc.warhead_thermobaric=HBM thermobaric payload effect.
cruise.detail.warhead_thermobaric=Contact or delayed fuse; no airburst.
cruise.desc.warhead_penetrator=Heavy payload with delayed game detonation.
cruise.detail.warhead_penetrator=Requires delayed fuse. Not for the light body.
cruise.desc.warhead_cluster=HBM cluster effect instead of ordinary HE.
cruise.detail.warhead_cluster=Contact, delayed or airburst fuse.
cruise.desc.warhead_emp=Creates the standard HBM EMP effect.
cruise.detail.warhead_emp=Effect depends on each device's HBM EMP support.
cruise.desc.fuse_contact=Activates on a block or non-friendly entity impact.
cruise.detail.fuse_contact=Full detonation is not repeated after save/reload.
cruise.desc.fuse_delay=Detonates 10 game ticks after impact.
cruise.detail.fuse_delay=Required for a penetrating payload.
cruise.desc.fuse_airburst=Activates 10 blocks above the designated target.
cruise.detail.fuse_airburst=HE, cluster or EMP only. Target Y ≤ 245.
cruise.desc.launch_booster=Launch from a ground fixture after a command.
cruise.detail.launch_booster=Requires folding wings; booster detaches after launch.
cruise.desc.launch_air=Launch after release from F-16, Su-27 or Tu-95.
cruise.detail.launch_air=Program the missile before loading the carrier.
cruise.desc.launch_rail=Light missile-drone release from a ground rail.
cruise.detail.launch_rail=Load first, then issue a separate launch command.
cruise.desc.link_autonomous=Executes the saved program without external updates.
cruise.detail.link_autonomous=Program cannot be changed after launch.
cruise.desc.link_command=Allows the owner to update an airborne missile program.
cruise.detail.link_command=Up to 4000 blocks, with fuel reserve and no strong jamming.
